{
  "about": "Every Mega Evolution the app knows, read by MegaForms. A form is triggered by holding its stone, or, with no stone, by knowing requires_move (Mega Rayquaza). species_key is the base species, normalized like BattleSimSeed.normalize. stone must name a HeldItem case. Base stats omit HP, which Mega Evolution never changes. ability is the engine's ability ID. origin is informational; see sources.",
  "sources": {
    "mainline": "Mega Evolutions from X/Y and Omega Ruby / Alpha Sapphire.",
    "legends-za": "Stats and abilities from the bundled champions-m-a-learnsets.json. Type changes (Mega Aggron dropping Rock; Mega Feraligatr and Mega Meganium gaining a second type) follow Z-A canon; species without an announced type change keep their base typing.",
    "champions-m-b": "Champions-original Megas. Stats and abilities from Serebii's pokedex-champions pages; stone names from game8.co's M-B item list. Their new abilities have no engine effect until computeAbilityModifiers ports them.",
    "champions-m-c": "Stats, types and abilities from Serebii's pokedex-champions pages. Golisopod and Baxcalibur are new; Garchomp, Lucario and Absol gain a second 'Z' Mega beside their original. New abilities (e.g. aura-guard) have no engine effect until ported."
  },
